    <title>Setting User Preferences</title>
  </head>
  <body bgcolor="#ffffff">
    <h1>
       <img width="32" height="32" src="../../images/carmenHelpIcons/c2_32.gif" border="0" hspace=
      "0">&nbsp;Setting User Preferences
    </h1>
    <hr width="100%" align="left" color="blue" size="2">
    <p>
       Each user can set up some values of certain CARMEN internal properties. Those properties,
      known as "User Preferences", are accessible through a dialog panel in the main menu
      (Tools/Carmen Configuration) and are finally stored in the own user registry (operating
      system independent).
    </p>
    <p>
       <img src="../../images/screens/CARMEN User Preferences Main Screen.jpg">&nbsp;
    </p>
    <h3>
       What properties could a user set up
    </h3>
    <p>
       The properties a user could set up or modify are:
    </p>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Colors for the nodes (chance,decision and utility nodes)
      </li>
      <li>
        Colors for the table cells
      </li>
      <li>
        Directories where application languages are located
      </li>
      <li>
        Initial relative position of the CARMEN&nbsp;main window
      </li>
      <li>
        Initial size of the CARMEN&nbsp;Help window
      </li>
      <li>
        User language
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
    <h3>
       Default properties
    </h3>
    <p>
       In other hand, if CARMEN&nbsp;is started at a first time and, therefore, there are not
      specific user preferences, the program creates a default configuration what every user can
      retrieve at any time from the Configuration Dialog, if required, using the button ("Reset
      preferences").
    </p>
    <p>
       These default properties are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Colors for the nodes (chance,decision and utility nodes)
      </li>
      <li>
        Colors for the table cells
      </li>
      <li>
        Directories where application languages are located
      </li>
      <li>
        Initial relative position of the CARMEN&nbsp;main window
      </li>
      <li>
        Initial size of the CARMEN&nbsp;Help window
      </li>
      <li>
        User language
      </li>
      <li>
        Last open files (reset to none)
      </li>
      <li>
        Last time that application were opened
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
    <h3>
       Advanced properties
    </h3>
    <p>
       Finally, there a set of properties that are only accessible for an advanced users or
      developers and there are not accessible from the previous dialog.
    </p>
    <p>
       These properties are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Window positions
      </li>
      <li>
        Font sizes
      </li>
      <li>
        Visual objects sizes
      </li>
      <li>
        Configuration for the options in Working panels
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
